            "kira_final": "Done. Summary:\n\n**Recovered DAG** (PC skeleton gave exactly 6 edges; U has no parents; remaining undirected edges oriented alphabetically child-first):\n- U→Y, U→R, U→D, U→M, D→Y, R→M\n\n**Outputs:**\n- `/app/learned_dag.csv` — the 6 edges in `to,from` format\n- `/app/intervened_dag.csv` — same structure (do-intervention doesn't change edges)\n- `/app/final_bn_sample.csv` — 10,000 samples with columns U,Y,R,D,M\n\nThe intervention do(Y=0) was implemented by replacing Y's CPD with a degenerate distribution (β=0, std=1e−9). Verification: Y is ~0 in all samples (std ≈ 0), while its former parents U and D remain sampled from the original distributions, confirming the causal cut of incoming edges into Y worked correctly.",
